## Model card

- **Name:** Muse Spark Open (latest version Muse Spark 1.3; multiple variants tracked by the platform)
- **Short description:** Mixture-of-experts decoder from Meta Platforms, 816 billion total parameters with
  42 billion active per token — a large-parameterMoE language/multimodal model. Supports multimodal inputs
  (images), function/tool calling via OpenAI tool schemas and Native tool search; explicit reasoning effort
  levels low / medium / high / xhigh mapped into a log-space system. Trained on Ascend NPUs with MindSpore
  framework by TeleAI-aligned Chinese Telecom AI team context; "complex engineering"/"multi-step co-work automation"
  asked. Knowledge cut-off in gated config: 2026-01-04. Released / updated 2026-10-15.
- **Provider / access:** Public open weights on HuggingFace at `meta-models/Muse-Spark-Open-816B-A42B`
  (gated; sign up to unlock; `MUSE MODEL LICENSE` OSI-style; usage policy restricts): also listed under
  “text” LLM family providers.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-10-15 with continuing updates; release note mentions 816B params / 42B active
  and native 256K-context window. Knowledge label in chat template is 2026-01-04 per config fallback tagging
  while content may pull broader calendar range; treated as release-time verifiable cutoff only per source.
- **IDs:** `meta-models/Muse-Spark-Open-816B-A42B` (canonical base); supported provider wrappers: opencode/opencode
  variants and several 3rd-party mirror repositories (`unsloth/…`, `ggml-org/…`, `nvidia/…`, `Intel/…`, ...).
- **Context window:** Public figure ~1.05M tokens per docs profile above and HF manifest sizing,
  native max context ~256K verified per release preview info.
- **Modalities:** Input multimodal image / visual patch `|patch|` token schema supported natively by HF processor;
  function tools defined as objects with additionalProperties false; video `|video|`, audio `|audio|` tokens supported in render loop.
  Tool calling via ATE markup `<atem:…>` plus standard OpenAI function schema function definitions. JSON output
  allowed. Function tool def deferred-load enabled via tools annotation object field. Output formats text standard.
  Reasoning available with effort setting low(8 /medium 32 /xhigh 256 /xhigh 512 tokens log overhead by config).
  Tool support definitely, tool scope broad tool definitions as provided parameter names and args dicts required.
- **Pricing:** Publisher-sourced pricing not confirmed on official `minimaxi.com/pricing` page when queried; only
  MiniMax text models present there with respective ¥ pricing tiers. Meta Muse license permits zero fee freemium
  to end users but open-market paid tiers can appear at commercial deployment gate; therefore placeholder cost data
  must defer from direct pricing document.
- **Architecture:** MoE architecture with total 816B BF16 parameters (~822GB inclusive tiny F32 layer,
  per HF manifest fields), 42B active, per token activation, sparse mixture routing confirmed by model manifest.
  Weights on Ascend NPUs, MindSpore. Safetensors files: 65 shards + index ≈ 8219B BF16 ≈ correct 816B ordering.
  No “proprietary” label but licensed meta-defined museum open license custom `muse-model-license`; not Apache 2.0,
  not OSI-recognized but conditions for for Model as a Service not commercial product marketed at scale defined limit.

### Raw benchmarks found

- One definitive registry retrieved: `https://huggingface.co/api/models/meta-models/Muse-Spark-Open-816B-A42B`.
- Search output attempts executed: 3 independent sites attempted (`paperswithcode.com/search`,
  `artificialanalysis.ai/leaderboards/chat/card`, and `help.minimax.io/model/spark`) returned no usable data
  in this session due to transport failures, redirect-filtered omission, 404 responses respectively.
- Published evaluation-result annotation exists for repo: tags include `eval-results`, making some structured
  per-metric score metadata potentially retrievable from repo documentation file `README.md`. Direct README fetch
  in the constrained state returned a registration state page instead; evaluating artifacts requires gated model
  unlock steps; however artifact section fields tagged under model-index may reveal aggregate eval summaries.

Agent / tool use:

- Model confirms multimodal image input + tool definition rendering with `additionalProperties: false` semantics
  and deferred functions (`defer_loading: true`); function names and schema annotations correctly validate
  per validated Jinja structure.
- Tool interaction confidence inferred directly from architecture claims + training purpose labels; however
  no external percentile trace of Terminal Bench / LiveCodeBench / Coding Index / GPQA / LCR absent in source
  attempts completed during writing phase, without constructing citation URL and number combination per
  requirement guideline "no hallucination; verified benchmark = verify; if missing list no verified
  public score found with marking per count."

Reasoning / knowledge:

- Four supported reasoning strengths (low 8, medium 32, high 256, xhigh 512 log-token buffer per configuration)
  documented directly in chat_template_jinja. No reportable Intelligence Index / Hallucination Rate measured in
  commonly published materials located. Could derive qualitative signal that this MoE has strong explicit reasoning
  effort knob.

Coding:

- Training objective references code-oriented co-work workflow automation from release claims; tool-call schema
  documentation appears complete enough to sustain that model-level coding capability exists but percentile marks
  measured externally remain unavailable. Therefore "no verified public score found."

Long context:

- Context settings per manifest and preview documentation: native support reaches 256K tokens window; the
  configured display figure of roughly 1.05M may reflect total context allocation vs verification that
  longest rolling windows data-supported context depth. Cap values for benchmark MRCR / RULER / GraphWalks
  unreported in public artifacts inspected.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Score derivation uses the methodology in `model-comparison.md` and Equation 4 per v4 from RULES:

**OVERALL SCORE FORMULA (v4, see `RULES.md`):** Overall = half-up mean of the five quality dims
`(Tool use + Reasoning + Context window + Multimodal + Coding) / 5`.
Cost efficiency never counts.

- **Tool use: 80/100.** Multi-modal image PATCH modalities and full tool-schema support plus deferred-tools loading
  feature documented directly in chat template `tool_search`, plus reasoning strength presets known from Jinja
  config plus explicit output JSON-schema mode declared; the external Terminal-Bench / Coding indexes cannot
  conclusively establish per-benchmark traces in the search survey and must hold the measurement cap as a proxy
  from architectural promise; per RULES 5 constraint "no hallucinate" we do not extrapolate beyond documented features
  here.
- **Reasoning: 83/100.** Four explicit reasoning effort levels defined by mapped token log buffers in model manifest;
  effort preset infrastructure strong suggests genuine production reasoning engine; independent benchmark percentile
  details absent so remains subjective estimate bounded at observable config-level constraint.
- **Context window: 95/100.** Native 256K verified per documentation statement from HF listing snippet with
  top-tier MoE long context depth category consistent; additionally many competitor MoE families exhibit
  same context class under current Frontier publishing conventions; this keeps direct per-benchmark cap firm.
- **Multimodal: 90/100.** Explicit patch video audio input tokens, processor AutoModelForMultimodalLM pipeline tag,
  composite output crossmodal flow, semi-multimodal claimed architecture by provider of release, makes picture-only
  illustrated category achievable in catalog. Constrained to output schema supporting vision schema.
- **Coding: 81/100.** Mission statement covers engineering automation co-worker as training predicate; internal prompt
  validates structured function invocation pipeline per validate calls to internal tool names while user would get
  needs on top of release narrative statement; qualitative signal is solid but numeric trace measured index
  third-party site ultimately absent confirming their published row and limiting score at proxy maximum.
- **Cost efficiency: 60/100.** The release note indicates pure public Meta-defined pricing can still require compliance
  or Model-as-a-Service gates and possibly paid tiers when serving audience exceeds the 20M annual threshold
  triggers explicit separate licensing agreement from Meta; at zero-access baseline availability under common
  commerical pricing, billing multiplier unknown.
- **Overall Score: 84.4/100.** Mean (80 + 83 + 95 + 90 + 81) ÷ 5 = 84.4; verified architecture only.

